 "_about": "Seconds each test file takes in one CI shard (setup + call + teardown, coverage on). scripts/ci_test_shards.py balances the shards on these; a file not listed weighs its test count times per_test_seconds_default. Measured 2026-10-09 per file from the shard reports of two CI runs of PR #72, both Python versions (run 37977024248 on d43f6edf and run 37983043056 on 5bd8c435): each file's LARGEST measurement, so a slower runner or Python version never under-weighs it. The refresh added the 44 test files written since the last one, which had grown to a tenth of a run's seconds and failed the aggregator on 5bd8c435. (The first table, 2026-09-27, spread each 72-test progress line's elapsed time evenly over its tests, which gave a slow file's seconds to its neighbours: P-740.) Refresh: download the test-shard-py* artifacts of one or more CI runs, both Python versions, and run `python3 scripts/ci_test_shards.py weights <every shard-*.json>`: it keeps each file's largest measurement, never a sum. The required test (py...) aggregators fail when the table goes stale.",
